  "strategyNotes": [
    "Diaries are written in plain form (〜た、〜だった). Do not be thrown by the lack of です/ます.",
    "〜と思っていたが (I had thought, but...) signals that reality was different. The contrast is usually tested.",
    "Passive 言われた means the writer RECEIVED the instruction. The teacher is the one speaking."
